      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><h3>Cost Matrix for Hyderabad to Blue Dart: A Breakdown of Factors</h3>

<p>When shipping goods from Hyderabad to Blue Dart, customers encounter various costs involved in the process. These costs comprise a comprehensive cost matrix, which includes base freight, fuel surcharge, packaging fees, insurance premium, and optional services.</p>
<p>To assist customers in understanding these components, we present the cost matrix in a clear and structured manner, highlighting how each cost is calculated and explaining why it matters for KPHB Colony, Hyderabad, to Blue Dart customers.</p>

<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Base Freight:</strong> This cost represents the initial fee charged for the carriage of goods from Hyderabad to Blue Dart. Base freight is determined based on the following factors:</span></li>
</ul>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Dimension-based pricing:</strong> The size and weight of the consignment are taken into account when calculating the base freight.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Geographical distance:</strong> The distance between Hyderabad and the destination in Blue Dart plays a significant role in determining the base freight cost.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Carrier:</strong> The shipping carrier selected by the customer determines the base freight fee.</span></li>
</ul>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Fuel Surcharge:</strong> The fuel surcharge is a variable cost that adjusts based on the fluctuations in fuel prices. It is added to the base freight to compensate for the increased cost of fuel. The formula for calculating the fuel surcharge is:</span></li>
</ul>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Fuel Surcharge = (Fuel Price - Base Fuel Price) / Base Fuel Price * Base Freight</strong></span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The Base Fuel Price is a benchmark provided by shipping carriers, while the Fuel Price is the current market price of fuel.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span>The resulting surcharge is then applied to the base freight.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Pricing matrix:</strong> The fuel surcharge is generally incorporated into the pricing matrix, with varying percentages based on the current fuel prices.</span></li>
</ul>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Packaging Fees:</strong> Packaging fees are charged in case the consignment requires additional packaging materials from the carrier. These fees cover the cost of materials like boxes, foam, and bubble wrap.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Dimension-Based Pricing:</strong> Packaging fees are typically calculated based on the weight and size of the package, as measured by the length, width, and height.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Packaging Requirements:</strong> Packaging fees are applied when the consignment's volume exceeds certain dimensions or when the package requires enhanced packaging to ensure safe transportation.</span></li>
<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Fee calculation:</strong> Packaging fees are calculated as: Packaging Fee = (Dimension Difference / Dimension Difference Threshold) * Base Freight</span></li>
</ul></div>
